Third-party code redistributed in this repository
-------------------------------------------------

vendor/dss-codec/
  The Rust DSS/DS2 decoder crate (also the source of the native `dss-decode`
  binary built by the Dockerfile, and of the in-browser decoder in web/).
  A copy of https://github.com/Guillain-RDCDE/dss-codec, a fork of
  https://github.com/hirparak/dss-codec (Kieran Hirpara, with contributions
  from Gaspard Petit, Patrick Domack and others).
  License: MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Kieran Hirpara - vendor/dss-codec/LICENSE,
  except these files, which are ports of FFmpeg code and keep its licence,
  LGPL-2.1-or-later (each says so in its header):
  - src/codec/dss_sp.rs: FFmpeg's libavcodec/dss_sp.c (c) 2014 Oleksij
    Rempel, with Patrick Domack's variable rate SP (format 1) from his fork;
  - src/demux/dss.rs: the block walk of libavformat/dss.c as Patrick
    Domack's fork has it (c) 2014 Oleksij Rempel and contributors;
  The crate built from them is distributed under the LGPL's terms for those
  files; its source is this repository.
  src/codec/g723_1.rs and src/tables/g723_1.rs (the G.723.1 decoder, for LP)
  are not a port: they are our own clean-room implementation of ITU-T
  Recommendation G.723.1, MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Guillain d'Erceville,
  written from docs/g723-1/SPEC.md and the Recommendation's text (see
  docs/19-the-last-format.md). Until October 2026 these two files were a
  port of FFmpeg's G.723.1 decoder (LGPL); that version is in this
  repository's history only.

vendor/dss-codec-wasm/
  The wasm-bindgen wrapper around the crate above. Adapted from
  https://github.com/gaspardpetit/dss-codec-wasm (Gaspard Petit): the
  dependency points at ../dss-codec, and the format list also covers DSS LP.
  License: MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Gaspard Petit - vendor/dss-codec-wasm/LICENSE

