Sample audio files
------------------

ffmpeg-upstream/fate/*.ds2, *.dss, and their copies in vendor/test_files/
  Short public test recordings used as regression fixtures (provenance in
  examples/README.md and ffmpeg-upstream/). They are not client recordings.

vendor/dss-codec/tests/fixtures/
  A public Grundig DSS-SP sample and the reference WAV produced from it by the
  genuine Grundig decoder, used to check that ours is bit-exact. Copied from
  the dss-codec fork above.
  olympus-*.dss / olympus-*.ds2: Patrick Domack's FATE samples (FFmpeg fork,
  release n9.0.2b): ten seconds of "Composed upon Westminster Bridge" by
  William Wordsworth, read for LibriVox (archive.org item
  shortpoetry_026_librivox, public domain), encoded with Olympus's ODMS R8
  encoder in SP, variable rate SP and LP. *.g723pk are the G.723.1 packets of
  the LP file, and synthetic packets, for the G.723.1 test.
  negative-lsp.g723pk: eight G.723.1 frames he sent on DS2-Anywhere#9,
  which once made the LP decoder panic.
  olympus-*-empty-lp.*, olympus-sp-empty-qp.ds2: four more of his FATE
  samples, from release n9.0.2c (an empty LP or QP block in front of the
  audio).


